            "body": "Ila ek digital audio-signal engineer hai. Jab ek smooth analog sound wave x computer mein jaati hai, to quantizer chip use do hisson mein tod deti hai:\n- Step level: **[x]** (Greatest Integer ≤ x)\n- Quantization error (sawtooth wave): **{x} = x - [x]** (hamesha 0 ≤ {x} < 1!)\n\nIla ne notice kiya ki jab x ek negative non-integer hota hai — jaise x = -2.3 — to [-2.3] = -3 hota hai (-2 nahi!), isliye [2.3] + [-2.3] = 2 + (-3) = **-1** aata hai (0 nahi)! Yehi chhoti si property advanced floor-function equations ki sabse badi key hai!",
            "bodyHinglish": "Ila ek digital audio-signal engineer hai. Jab ek smooth analog sound wave x computer mein jaati hai, to quantizer chip use do hisson mein tod deti hai:\n- Step level: **[x]** (Greatest Integer ≤ x)\n- Quantization error (sawtooth wave): **{x} = x - [x]** (hamesha 0 ≤ {x} < 1!)\n\nIla ne notice kiya ki jab x ek negative non-integer hota hai — jaise x = -2.3 — to [-2.3] = -3 hota hai (-2 nahi!), isliye [2.3] + [-2.3] = 2 + (-3) = **-1** aata hai (0 nahi)! Yehi chhoti si property advanced floor-function equations ki sabse badi key hai!"
