            "body": "| Topic | Mukhya vishay | Khaas formula / yaad rakhne ki baat |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Topic 1** | Directed Angles, Degrees & Radians | π rad = 180°; 1° = 60′, 1′ = 60″; **l = rθ** (θ hamesha radians mein!). |\n| **Topic 2** | Unit Circle, ASTC, Allied Angles & Graphs | P = (cos x, sin x); ASTC; π, 2π par no change, π/2, 3π/2 par change; sin, cos ∈ [−1, 1] (period 2π); tan period π. |\n| **Topic 3** | Compound Angles (x ± y) | cos(x ± y) = cos x cos y ∓ sin x sin y; sin(x ± y) = sin x cos y ± cos x sin y; tan(π/4 ± x) = (1 ± tan x)/(1 ∓ tan x). |\n| **Topic 4** | Multiple, Half-Angle & C–D Identities | sin 2x = 2 sin x cos x; cos 2x = 2 cos² x − 1 = 1 − 2 sin² x; 1 ± cos x = 2 cos²/sin²(x/2); cos C − cos D = −2 sin((C+D)/2) sin((C−D)/2). |\n| **Topic 5** | Trigonometric Equations | Principal in [0, 2π); sin x = sin y ⟹ nπ + (−1)ⁿ y; cos x = cos y ⟹ 2nπ ± y; tan x = tan y ⟹ nπ + y; hamesha factor karo! |\n| **Topic 6** | Mixed Applications & Synthesis | Symmetric pairing in C–D; a cos x + b sin x = c ko √(a² + b²) se bhaag do (range [−√(a² + b²), +√(a² + b²)]). |\n\n**Aage kya?** Agle chapter **Complex Numbers and Quadratic Equations** mein hum us sawaal ka jawab kholenge jise Class 10 mein \"no real roots\" keh kar chhod diya tha — **√(−1) = i** ki naye imaginary numbers ki duniya!",
