            "bodyHinglish": "Topic 2 mein humne complex number z = x + iy ko Argand plane par rectangular coordinates (x, y) se dikhaya. Par kisi point ka pata batane ka ek doosra, behad sundar tareeka bhi hai — **origin se uski seedhi doori (r)** aur **positive real axis se uska angle (θ)**! Isi ko **Polar Form** kehte hain. Is topic mein hum kisi bhi complex number ko (chahe wo kisi bhi quadrant ya axis par ho) polar form **r(cos θ + i sin θ)** mein badalna aur **Principal Argument** nikaalna seekhenge."
