            "body": "Topic 1 mein humne baar-baar 4 × 3 × 2 × 1 ya 5 × 4 × 3 jaise ghatte hue products likhe. Maths ne inhe chhota likhne ke liye **Factorial (n!)** aur **Permutation (ⁿPᵣ)** ka symbol banaya. Jab cheezon ko kisi **khaas kram (order)** mein sajana ho — jaise shelf par trophies, line mein students, ya kisi shabd ke letters — to har alag arrangement ek **Permutation** kehlata hai! Is topic mein hum Factorial (including **0! = 1 kyun?**), **ⁿPᵣ**, identical objects ke permutations (**ALLAHABAD**), aur **Bundle (Together)** aur **Gap (Never Together)** tricks seekhenge.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Topic 1 mein humne baar-baar 4 × 3 × 2 × 1 ya 5 × 4 × 3 jaise ghatte hue products likhe. Maths ne inhe chhota likhne ke liye **Factorial (n!)** aur **Permutation (ⁿPᵣ)** ka symbol banaya. Jab cheezon ko kisi **khaas kram (order)** mein sajana ho — jaise shelf par trophies, line mein students, ya kisi shabd ke letters — to har alag arrangement ek **Permutation** kehlata hai! Is topic mein hum Factorial (including **0! = 1 kyun?**), **ⁿPᵣ**, identical objects ke permutations (**ALLAHABAD**), aur **Bundle (Together)** aur **Gap (Never Together)** tricks seekhenge."
