            "body": "Purnima ek insurance firm mein actuarial analyst hai. Ek risk model mein (3 + 2x)⁹ ke terms alag-alag claim scenarios darshate the, jahan x = 1/2 tha.\nIntern ne socha: \"n = 9 ka middle term T₅ aur T₆ sabse bada hoga!\"\nPurnima ne roka: \"Middle term sirf tab sabse bada hota hai jab a = b ho! Yahan a = 3 aur b = 2(1/2) = 1 alag-alag hain! Ratio test **|Tᵣ₊₁ / Tᵣ| ≥ 1** lagao: m = (9 + 1)(1/3) / (1 + 1/3) = (10/3)/(4/3) = 2.5 => sabse bada term **T₃** hai (T₅ nahi!)!\"",
            "bodyHinglish": "Purnima ek insurance firm mein actuarial analyst hai. Ek risk model mein (3 + 2x)⁹ ke terms alag-alag claim scenarios darshate the, jahan x = 1/2 tha.\nIntern ne socha: \"n = 9 ka middle term T₅ aur T₆ sabse bada hoga!\"\nPurnima ne roka: \"Middle term sirf tab sabse bada hota hai jab a = b ho! Yahan a = 3 aur b = 2(1/2) = 1 alag-alag hain! Ratio test **|Tᵣ₊₁ / Tᵣ| ≥ 1** lagao: m = (9 + 1)(1/3) / (1 + 1/3) = (10/3)/(4/3) = 2.5 => sabse bada term **T₃** hai (T₅ nahi!)!\""
