            "heading": "Part A: Parametric (Distance) Form Of A Line (\"Kyun\"!)",
            "headingHinglish": "Part A: Parametric (Distance) Form Of A Line (\"Kyun\"!)",
            "body": "Maan lo ek line point P(x₁, y₁) se guzarti hai aur positive x-axis se inclination θ (0° ≤ θ < 180°) banati hai.\nIs line par P se signed distance **r** door koi bhi point Q(x, y) lo:\n- Horizontal step: x - x₁ = r cos θ\n- Vertical step: y - y₁ = r sin θ\n\nIsliye **Parametric Form**:\n**(x - x₁) / cos θ = (y - y₁) / sin θ = r**\nyaani **x = x₁ + r cos θ**, **y = y₁ + r sin θ**!\n- **+r** aage (upar/right) ka point deta hai aur **-r** peechhe (neeche/left) ka exact point deta hai!",
            "bodyHinglish": "Maan lo ek line point P(x₁, y₁) se guzarti hai aur positive x-axis se inclination θ (0° ≤ θ < 180°) banati hai.\nIs line par P se signed distance **r** door koi bhi point Q(x, y) lo:\n- Horizontal step: x - x₁ = r cos θ\n- Vertical step: y - y₁ = r sin θ\n\nIsliye **Parametric Form**:\n**(x - x₁) / cos θ = (y - y₁) / sin θ = r**\nyaani **x = x₁ + r cos θ**, **y = y₁ + r sin θ**!\n- **+r** aage (upar/right) ka point deta hai aur **-r** peechhe (neeche/left) ka exact point deta hai!"
